{"name":"Blueberry Lemonade","hex":"#d01343","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blueberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edible round berry, belonging to the cowberry group (Vaccinium sect. Cyanococcus), with flared crowns at the end, that turns blue on ripening.","The shrub of the above-mentioned berry."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark blue colour.","Resembling or characteristic of blueberries."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blueberry"},{"term":"lemonade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flavored beverage consisting of water, lemon, and sweetener, sometimes ice, served mainly as a refreshment.","A clear, usually carbonated, beverage made from lemon or artificial lemon flavouring, water, and sugar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemonade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blueberry","blocks":[{"text":"Blueberries are a widely distributed and widespread group of perennial flowering plants with blue or purple berries. They are classified in the section Cyanococcus within the genus Vaccinium. Commercial blueberries—both wild (lowbush) and cultivated (highbush)—are all native to North America. The highbush varieties were introduced into Europe during the 1930s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Blueberries.jpg/330px-Blueberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blueberry","wikidata":"Q13178"},{"title":"Lemonade","blocks":[{"text":"Lemonade is a sweetened lemon-flavored drink that may be carbonated or un-carbonated; when carbonated, it is sometimes called a lemon soda. There are many varieties of lemonade found throughout the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Lemonade_-_27682817724.jpg/330px-Lemonade_-_27682817724.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki